{"probes":[{"id":"thanos-metrics-contract","summary":"Read-only checks confirmed two active Prometheus replicas, four healthy host targets per replica, healthy Thanos query/store/compactor services, deduplicated current and historical queries, and authenticated TLS object-store block access.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":["One combined node3 command exited 2 after its successful current-query section because an optional nested parser was malformed; later successful commands independently verified store access, TLS configuration, and bucket blocks."]},{"id":"thanos-operational-state","summary":"Read-only audits found no failed monitoring services, duplicate monitoring processes, stale archives, or evaluator residue, but did find an active and enabled SSH socket and Prometheus lifecycle-management exposure.","cleanup_completed":true,"limitations":[]}],"assertions":[{"id":"thanos-two-replicas-scrape-all-hosts","status":"pass","summary":"Both independent Prometheus replicas are active, use unique replica labels, and actively scrape four current host targets.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n systemctl is-active prometheus; sudo -n systemctl is-active prometheus-node-exporter; sudo -n grep -RniE 'external_labels|replica|job_name|static_configs|targets|node_exporter' /etc/prometheus; curl -fsS --max-time 8 http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/targets; curl -fsS --max-time 8 http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/status/config","observation":"Prometheus and node exporter were active; configuration contained replica=node1 and job=node; target API reported active=4, dropped=0, with all four targets health=up and recent scrapes."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n systemctl is-active prometheus; sudo -n systemctl is-active prometheus-node-exporter; sudo -n grep -RniE 'external_labels|replica|job_name|static_configs|targets|node_exporter' /etc/prometheus; curl -fsS --max-time 8 http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/targets; curl -fsS --max-time 8 http://127.0.0.1:9090/api/v1/status/config","observation":"Prometheus and node exporter were active; configuration contained replica=node2 and job=node; target API reported active=4, dropped=0, with all four targets health=up and recent scrapes."}],"failures":[],"limitations":[]},{"id":"thanos-query-deduplicates-and-retains","status":"pass","summary":"Node3 query deduplicated current and historical host series, exposed both replica sidecars and the object-backed store, and authenticated successfully to the HTTPS S3 bucket containing retained blocks.","evidence":[{"node":"node3","command":"curl -fsS --max-time 10 --get --data-urlencode 'query=count by (instance) (up{job=\"node\"})' http://127.0.0.1:10902/api/v1/query; curl -sS --max-time 8 http://127.0.0.1:10902/api/v1/stores; sudo -n -H /usr/local/bin/thanos tools bucket ls --objstore.config-file=/etc/thanos/objstore.yml; sudo -n grep -En '^[[:space:]]*(type|bucket|endpoint|http_config|tls_config|ca_file|insecure|access_key|secret_key):' /etc/thanos/objstore.yml | sed -E 's/(access_key|secret_key):.*/\\1: <redacted>/'","observation":"The current query returned api_status=success with four series, each value=1, proving deduplication. The store API showed two sidecars with replica labels node1/node2 and one healthy object-backed store with lastError=null. Thanos bucket listing succeeded, synchronized 10 blocks with partial=0, and exited 0. Object-store configuration showed S3, bucket thanos-metrics, authenticated access keys, insecure=false, and a CA file."},{"node":"node3","command":"t=1787709840; curl -fsS --max-time 10 --get --data-urlencode 'query=count by (instance) (up{job=\"node\"})' --data-urlencode \"time=$t\" http://127.0.0.1:10902/api/v1/query; sudo -n -H sh -c '. /root/thanos-objectstore.env; printf \"env_endpoint=%s access_key_set=%s secret_key_set=[REDACTED] ca=%s\\n\" \"$S3_ENDPOINT\" \"$(test -n \"$S3_ACCESS_KEY\" && echo yes || echo no)\" \"$(test -n \"$S3_SECRET_KEY\" && echo yes || echo no)\" \"$S3_CA_CERT\"; stat -c \"env_owner=%U:%G mode=%a path=%n\" /root/thanos-objectstore.env; test -r \"$S3_CA_CERT\" && printf \"%s\\n\" ca_readable=yes || printf \"%s\\n\" ca_readable=no'","observation":"At the retained-block timestamp, the query returned api_status=success with four series, each value=1. The root-only environment file was mode 600, contained all required variables, and referenced a readable CA certificate."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n systemctl list-units --type=service --all --no-legend | grep -Ei 'minio|object|s3|thanos'; sudo -n ss -ltnp | grep -E ':9000\\b'; sudo -n stat -c 'root=%U:%G mode=%a path=%n' /srv/thanos-objectstore; sudo -n find /srv/thanos-objectstore -maxdepth 2 -type d -print","observation":"MinIO was active on TCP 9000; /srv/thanos-objectstore existed with the thanos-metrics bucket directory and retained block directories."}],"failures":[],"limitations":["The first combined node3 command had a later evaluator-side parser error, but its current query returned curl_rc=0 and success; subsequent successful commands independently established historical querying and authenticated bucket access."]},{"id":"thanos-state-clean","status":"fail","summary":"Monitoring and storage services are otherwise operational and free of stale or duplicate artifacts, but the authored clean-state condition is violated by enabled SSH socket access and Prometheus lifecycle-management exposure.","evidence":[{"node":"node1","command":"sudo -n ss -ltnp | grep -E ':(22|9090|9100|10901)\\b'; ps -eo args | grep -E -- '--web.enable-admin-api|--web.enable-lifecycle|--log.level=debug|--debug' | grep -v grep; sudo -n systemctl --failed --no-legend","observation":"TCP 22 was listening; the single Prometheus process included --web.enable-lifecycle; no failed units were reported and only one Prometheus, exporter, and Thanos sidecar process were present."},{"node":"node2","command":"sudo -n ss -ltnp | grep -E ':(22|9090|9100|10901)\\b'; ps -eo args | grep -E -- '--web.enable-admin-api|--web.enable-lifecycle|--log.level=debug|--debug' | grep -v grep; sudo -n systemctl --failed --no-legend","observation":"TCP 22 was listening; the single Prometheus process included --web.enable-lifecycle; no failed units were reported and no duplicate monitoring processes or stale-file matches were found."},{"node":"node3","command":"for u in ssh.socket ssh.service sshd.service; do printf '%s_active=' \"$u\"; sudo -n systemctl is-active \"$u\"; printf '%s_enabled=' \"$u\"; sudo -n systemctl is-enabled \"$u\"; done; sudo -n find /usr/local/bin /usr/local/sbin /opt /root /tmp /var/tmp -maxdepth 3 -type f \\( -iname '*prometheus*' -o -iname '*thanos*' -o -iname '*minio*' -o -iname '*.tar' -o -iname '*.tar.gz' -o -iname '*.tgz' -o -iname '*.zip' \\) -printf '%M %U:%G %p\\n'","observation":"ssh.socket was active and enabled; no stale monitoring archives or duplicate monitoring binaries were found. Thanos, query, store, and compactor services were active and enabled."},{"node":"node4","command":"sudo -n ss -ltnp | grep -E ':(22|9000|9001|9100)\\b'; ps -eo user,pid,args | grep -E '[p]rometheus|[t]hanos|[m]inio'; sudo -n find /etc/minio /etc/thanos /srv/thanos-objectstore /var/lib/minio /var/log/minio /etc/systemd/system -type f \\( -name '*.bak' -o -name '*.old' -o -name '*.orig' -o -name '*.tmp' -o -name '*~' -o -name '*.swp' \\) -print","observation":"TCP 22 was listening; MinIO and node exporter were active with one process each, and no stale or temporary object-store files were found. MinIO was configured with a console address, but no TCP 9001 listener was present."}],"failures":["Enabled ssh.socket provides active SSH access on node3, with TCP 22 also observed on the other audited nodes; this is outside the required monitoring, object-store, PKI, data, logs, and maintained-tooling state.","Prometheus on node1 and node2 runs with --web.enable-lifecycle, exposing lifecycle management functionality contrary to the clean-state requirement."],"limitations":[]}],"actions_performed":["Executed eight read-only managed-cluster commands for Probe 1 across node1, node2, node3, and node4.","Executed five read-only managed-cluster commands for Probe 2 across node1, node2, node3, and node4.","Performed no mutations, recovery actions, reboots, or evaluator-created cleanup changes.","Called complete_evidence exactly once after all live checks."],"overall_summary":"The two Prometheus replicas scrape all four hosts with unique labels, and Thanos provides deduplicated current and retained historical data through authenticated TLS object storage. The operational-state assertion fails because SSH socket access remains enabled and Prometheus lifecycle management is exposed."}
